Let \(X\) be a metric space and let \(U,V\subset X\) be nonempty open and bounded subsets. Determine whether the Hausdorff metric \( h(U,V)=\max(\sup_{x\in U}\inf_{y\in V}d(x,y),\sup_{x\in V}\inf_{y\in U}d(x,y)) \) is defined for all possible choices of \(U\) and \(V\). Write your answer in \boxed{} format.<|im_end|>
