3. Non-Constant Functions: If an antiholomorphic function has an interior maximum in its modulus, the function must be constant.

Examples like \( f(z) = \overline{z} \) and \( f(z) = \overline{z} + 1 \) on the unit disk confirm that the maximum modulus is attained on the boundary. Therefore, the Maximum Modulus Principle applies to antiholomorphic functions.

